<p>Opposition leader Péter Magyar and his centre-right Tisza party won a landslide in Hungary&#x27;s April 12 election, ending Viktor Orbán&#x27;s 16 years in office. Final results reported by The Straits Times gave Tisza 141 parliamentary seats, leaving Magyar with a strong governing majority. Magyar has cast the result as a chance for a fresh start at home and renewed ties with Europe, signaling possible shifts in both domestic politics and Hungary&#x27;s foreign policy direction.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_RjIgKCVxsx9EQhib0oiKznZ7SqLqwKL3UXLK0kkxTRTD7-MlSUtK0hd1Qv0_aXCPYxuzTswxranJ0PHmW-kv_bf5_IXs5R2_RLNyCWqDStmky7HnchNwLMmbPOhAjthCOHRBgLhvVaQWxg6kLP3dfM16qUFtg-02R9QFZJPISWxeT0wBWsLNkuo6g5Tiw' alt='Péter Magyar, the Tisza party leader who defeated Viktor Orbán in Hungary&#x27;s election' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Péter Magyar and Tisza: Magyar&#x27;s camp moved quickly after the election, presenting the result as a mandate for immediate governing and political change. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g40npz37lo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>The Hindu&#x27;s profile: The paper describes Magyar&#x27;s rise as unusual because he came from Orbán&#x27;s own political orbit, then used that background to challenge the long-ruling system from within the broader centre-right. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/peter-magyar-the-former-loyalist-who-toppled-victor-orban/article70868053.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>New York Times analysis: The Times emphasizes the scale of voter rejection of Orbán, portraying the result as a decisive break after 16 years of one leader&#x27;s dominance. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000010842261/who-is-the-new-leader-of-hungary.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000010842261/who-is-the-new-leader-of-hungary.html'>Who Is the New Leader of Hungary?</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g40npz37lo'>Orbán&#x27;s era was over in a flash and Hungary&#x27;s next PM is a man in a hurry</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/magyars-parliamentary-majority-in-hungary-increases-after-final-count'>Peter Magyar’s parliamentary majority in Hungary increases to 141 after final count</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/peter-magyar-the-former-loyalist-who-toppled-victor-orban/article70868053.ece'>Peter Magyar | From loyalist to rival</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>